# PHYSICAL CONSTRAINTS (Paul, 2 November 2026: "we start this process by locking physical constraints
# into a range of values"). A distance, a time or a count has limits the world sets: the gun's reach
# (60 tiles), the map (128 wide, 181 across, 256 the largest), a pillbox's ring (8), direct range and
# a tank's sight (10), a recon's (20), a shell's flight (6 s at full range), a reload (4 s, 12 s), the
# bay (2, 6, 3, 2), the squad (4), the material a tank carries (8), sixteen seats, a match of 30 min at
# most. These are ranges, not decrees: the search moves inside them. Where a number is a fact of the
# simulator (tree_material is 4 a tree; a fourth strike drone cannot launch) the range says so and the
# decree is Paul's to make. The week's reason: base_r walked 16, 32, 8, 6.15 in a day and coming_r
# reached 221 tiles on a 128-tile map.
